Subject: Gopher access to *new* campus newspaper articles
Message-ID: <C1tzp7.IK8@cs.uiuc.edu>
Date: Tue, 2 Feb 1993 17:10:18 GMT

If you have access to gopher, you can read new campus newspaper
articles. The articles come from many sources, but most are from the
U. of Illinois, the U. of Minnesota, and the U. of Texas.

To see them, try the command:

gopher gopher.eff.org 5070

Then choose

   "What's New in newspapers? (e.g.: 1 day 2 hours ago) <?>"

Then type, for example, "one day ago".

You will see all the newspaper articles that have been added to my
"whatsnew" list in the last 24 hours.


OPTIONAL

The last item you will see will look something like this:

   "**Bookmark for future new "newspapers" items (19930202161247 gophe../"

This is a timestamp. Save the it as a bookmark. The next time you want
to see what newspaper articles are new, simply view the bookmark (and
save the new timestamp as a bookmark).

- Carl

ANNOTATED REFERENCES

(All these documents are available on-line. Access information follows.)

=================
admin/whatsnewd
=================
* Code for and description of "whatsnewd" (v. 0.4)

(Connect your Gopher to "gopher.eff.org", port "5070" to play with it.)

It is a gopher-protocol server.

What it does:

When a user gives a date (e.g. "1 day ago") or enters a dated bookmark
(generated by a previous query), he or she gets a gopher menu of the
gopher items that are new or changed since that date.


=================
=================

If you have gopher, you can browse the CAF archive with the command
   gopher gopher.eff.org

These document(s) are also available by anonymous ftp (the preferred
method) and by email. To get the file(s) via ftp, do an anonymous ftp
to ftp.eff.org (192.88.144.4), and get file(s):

  pub/academic/admin/whatsnewd

To get the file(s) by email, send email to archive-server@eff.org.
Include the line(s) (be sure to include the space before the file
name):

send acad-freedom/admin whatsnewd

