The main reason system administrators log anonymous ftp activity, per
your description is for system security.  ftp is one of several common
points of attack by computer crackers and it makes good sense to
maintain logs in order to identify potential crackers, locate (and then
patch) security holes they may be trying to exploit, and in some instances,
collect information for future prosecution.

I've seen some very interesting ftp logs of cracking attempts over
the years.  Often one sees a lot of ftp users just making simple
mistakes or behaving "inappropropriately" because of naivete.
For instance, trying to read files so they can get email addresses
of people on a particular system; most people who try to do that
via ftp just don't understand that there are appropriate tools for
getting such info.  But sometimes you also see crackers up to the
same sorts of info gathering.

