certainly has many in-house uses.  I doubt that the "domestic intel-
ligence agencies" have much use for borrowers' records.

>Is logging a case of "the fascist big brother should have no business
>invading my privacy, and it's probably illegal collection of personal
>information in many countries"?

Your privacy stops at the digital doorway to their system.  I certainly
hope that ftp sites do not publicize their download/upload logs, but I
also understand the usefulness of that information.

