In article <sfarrell.728835419@unix2.tcd.ie> sfarrell@unix2.tcd.ie (Sean Farrell) writes:
>I think it'd be fair if the logs were treated the same as library records,
>and if any site operating a different policy informed the user of that fact.
>Thoughts?

50% agreement.  A site should make its policy on log information known to 
the user in advance.  Users should _not_ assume any default policy, anymore
than you can assume that statistics on your usenet posting activities would
be private.

The same guidelines apply to mailing lists, database entries, server logs, 
and interactive services.  If you don't see an explicit statement of policy,
don't presume that the operator shares a "common sense of responsibility"
with the raw data or even derived information.

Look at rfc1355 (Privacy and Accuracy issues in NIC DB's) for related
background information.

/John

