My prior disclimer still applies but note that is says "in THEIR
persons...papers, and effects".   My first point is that the property
in question is U of O's property. Not your property. Your right to
YOUR privacy only applies to YOUR effects. If the owner is someone
else, they can set terms which you must agree to in order to borrow
their property. The 4th amendment is not putting restrictions on what
owners may do with their property. If I am a cattle rancher, and we
